course: dictionary
lesson: 12061
title: Clarity
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clarity is a noun. It names the quality of being clear. It can mean something is easy to understand, easy to see through, or that your thinking is clear. «The teacher explained the sum with clarity.» The explanation was easy to follow, so the word clarity points to clear and easy to understand.
explain: Clarity can also describe water or pictures. «The water in the pond had great clarity, and we could see the fish swimming.» You could see right through the water, so clarity means being clear to see through. «The photo had sharp clarity, so every leaf was easy to see.» Here it means a clear, sharp picture.
explain: Clarity can mean clear thinking too. «After a good sleep, Mia had a moment of clarity and knew the answer.» The word moment tells you it was sudden, and the answer tells you her thoughts became clear. So a moment of clarity means a sudden, clear understanding.
fact: Clarity means being clear and easy to understand.
fact: Clarity can also mean being clear to see through, like clean water or a sharp picture.
fact: «For clarity» means to make something easier to understand.
fact: «With clarity» means in a clear way, so people can follow it.
fact: «A moment of clarity» means a sudden clear understanding of something.
exercise: «The teacher explained the sum with clarity.» What does clarity mean here? | Being loud and fast | *Being clear and easy to understand | Being sad about maths | Having lots of pencils
exercise: «The water in the pond had great clarity, and we could see the fish.» What does clarity describe? | Being cold and wet | Being very deep and dark | *Being clear enough to see through
exercise: Mia had a moment of clarity and knew the answer. What does moment of clarity mean? | *A sudden, clear understanding | A long, sleepy yawn | A wrong answer given in a rush | A time when the lights went out
test: «For clarity, the writer used short sentences.» What was the writer trying to do? | Draw a picture | Make the writing as long as possible | *Make the writing easy to understand | Hide the meaning
test: «The photo had great clarity, so every leaf was sharp.» What does clarity mean here? | *Clear, sharp detail you can see | Being loud | Being wet and blurry | Being very dark and grey
exam: «She wrote her plan with clarity, and everyone understood it.» What does clarity mean in this sentence? | Being angry at the plan | *Being clear and easy to understand | Being far away | Being a secret
